note draft

# SHELVED 2026-08-30, and the decision it is waiting on is written here rather than left implicit.
#
# This is a ROLE MANIFEST (`role book` / `take @/book/**`), not Term code, and nothing reads it: deck.tree declares
# no `role`, and projectRoleOf (deck/call/code/role-of.ts) looks only for `<root>/role.tree` or the path a manifest's
# `role` head names. So it was reached by exactly one thing, the build walk, which compiled it as code and reported
# its manifest heads as undefined NAMES (`role`, `book`) - the same false error a `deck.tree` gave before manifests
# were taken out of the walk.
#
# Two ways to settle it, and they are not the same:
#   - it is meant to BE @term/deck's role manifest, in which case it belongs at deck/role.tree (or deck.tree grows a
#     `role ./role` line), and the walk should skip it the way it skips deck.tree
#   - it is a FIXTURE for the role parser, in which case it belongs under test/ with the other fixtures
#
# Whoever knows which should move it and delete this marker. See package-builds-0006.

load @term/code
  find code
  find book

role book
  take @/book/**/*.tree
    miss @/book/**/\{code,view\}/**/*.tree

role code
  take @/code/**/*.tree
  # book can have nested code in it
  take @/book/**/\{code,view\}/**/*.tree
